{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SCOPE — started as \"resolve bugs 1803 and jira-reb-1582\" and grew, at operator direction, into: the structural link rule, the rebar doctor verb, a doctor-epic merge, and two follow-on defects the work exposed.\n\nWHAT LANDED (12 merged changes)\n\nStory affe-2b42-4ee4-4e12 (closed), two children:\n- 7ab3-9df0-7a90-4ffd — blocking-link comparability is STRUCTURAL, not type-tier. Nearest common ancestor with a virtual-root sentinel (so parentless tickets are siblings and there is no undefined disjoint case). _TYPE_TIER and its three helpers deleted; _get_ancestors uncapped + cycle-guarded; is_redundant recomputed from the RESOLVED pair, inside the resolver, so add_dependency / the dry-run preview / the standalone resolve path all inherit the ancestor refusal. Merged 693a6bf41.\n- 9ad7-d5a2-a664-4827 — the audit/repair check, shipped as `rebar doctor` (six changes: 1028, 1039, 1040, 1045, 1047, 1052).\n\nFollow-ons the work exposed, both closed:\n- fec5-d8bb-86cd-453e — link escalation was silent for library/MCP callers. Record now returns through five layers. Merged 1059 / 6f787da0529e.\n- 6e4f-cad1-aa39-446a — retyping a ticket replayed a verdict computed under different criteria. Merged 1058 / eea930a64e20.\n\nSuperseded bugs 1803 + jira-reb-1582 closed duplicate. Doctor epics merged: dabb-7d4b-f5bc-40e6 canonical, 18ae-4f54-a85b-4ddb closed duplicates.\n\nSTORE REMEDIATION — 18 legacy bad edges found on this tracker, 12 repaired, 8 residual and provably inert (every endpoint closed, so none can reach ready/next-batch). Pre-repair anchor tag at 962624641cae."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785448728809970001,"uuid":"b9324b4c-3fc7-441d-9698-4631dc3a8f45"}